## 8. Storage and File Management

Implement a controlled file storage mechanism.

Requirements:

- Store original uploaded documents.
- Store extracted images separately.
- Store extracted structured content.
- Generate unique IDs.
- Avoid filename collisions.
- Prevent path traversal.
- Do not expose internal filesystem paths through APIs.
- Configure upload storage using environment variables where appropriate.
- Implement safe temporary file cleanup.
- Keep original documents available for later reprocessing.

If the project already has a database, follow its existing persistence architecture. Do not introduce a new database unnecessarily.

## 9. Large Document Handling

Some users may upload documents containing hundreds of pages.

Requirements:

- Process documents page by page or in manageable sections.
- Avoid unnecessarily loading entire large documents into memory.
- Preserve source references during extraction.
- Set configurable file size and upload limits.
- Handle extraction failures at the page or file level.
- Prepare extracted content for future token-aware chunking.
- Avoid sending large documents to the LLM in this milestone.

Do not introduce RAG or vector databases at this stage.

## 10. Future Multimodal AI Integration

Prepare the architecture for a future AI requirement-understanding engine.

The next milestone should be able to send:

**Textual content:**
- Extracted document text.
- Headings and paragraphs.
- Structured tables.
- Spreadsheet data.
- User stories and acceptance criteria.

**Visual content:**
- Actual embedded screenshots.
- UI mockups.
- Flowcharts.
- Architecture diagrams.
- Rendered scanned PDF pages.

**Context:**
- Original filename.
- Page number.
- Section.
- Slide number.
- Sheet name.
- Image ID.
- Associated text.

The future multimodal LLM should be able to analyze the actual image alongside its relevant textual context.

Keep text extraction, image extraction, OCR and vision analysis as separate processing stages.

Do not implement fake AI image descriptions or fabricated vision-analysis results.

Do not integrate OpenAI vision analysis in this milestone unless it is already supported by existing code and can be implemented without expanding the scope.

## 11. Processing Status Management

Clearly distinguish the following statuses:

- Upload completed.
- Text extraction completed.
- Image extraction completed.
- OCR completed.
- OCR pending.
- Vision analysis completed.
- Vision analysis pending.
- Partially processed.
- Failed.

A document containing screenshots must never be reported as completely processed if only its text was extracted.

For example, if the text extraction succeeds but image extraction fails, report partial processing and include the relevant warning.

## 12. Security and Validation

Implement:

- File extension validation.
- MIME type validation.
- File signature validation wherever practical.
- File size limits.
- File count limits.
- Unique server-side filenames.
- Safe storage paths.
- Path traversal prevention.
- Protection against malformed files.
- Controlled temporary file cleanup.
- Safe error handling.
- No execution of uploaded files.

Do not expose stack traces, internal paths or sensitive server information in API responses.

